# =============================================================================
# frontend/.env — ConceptTree Frontend Configuration
# =============================================================================
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file:  cp .env.example .env
#   2. Adjust values only if your backend runs on a non-default port.
#   3. Vite exposes ONLY variables prefixed with VITE_ to browser code.
#      Variables without that prefix are ignored at build time.
#
# HOW THESE TWO VARIABLES WORK TOGETHER
#   In the browser, every API call goes to: <page-origin>/api/...
#   During development, Vite's dev server intercepts those /api/* requests
#   and forwards (proxies) them to VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET (the local backend).
#   This eliminates CORS errors in dev without changing any production behaviour,
#   because in production a reverse proxy (Nginx / cloud gateway) does the same job.
#
# Primary reader: Frontend developer running the app locally for the first time.
# =============================================================================

# Base path prepended to every API request made by the app.
# Keep as /api so the same axios/fetch code works in both dev (proxied by Vite)
# and production (proxied by Nginx or a cloud gateway).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# Dev-only: Vite forwards /api/* requests to this address during `npm run dev`.
# Must match the backend port in start-dev.sh (default 8000).
# This variable is NOT embedded in the production build — it only affects the dev server.
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8000
